---
import ToolLayout from '../../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import { toolBySlug } from '../../../lib/content/tools';
import { isLang, localePath } from '../../../lib/i18n';
if (!isLang(Astro.params.lang!)) return new Response(null, { status: 404 });
const lang = Astro.locals.lang; const fr = lang === 'fr'; const tool = toolBySlug('character-counter')!; const L = (p: string) => localePath(lang, p);
const limits = [['Facebook', 63206, 'fa-brands fa-facebook', '#1877F2'], ['Instagram', 2200, 'fa-brands fa-instagram', '#E4405F'], ['X (Twitter)', 280, 'fa-brands fa-x-twitter', '#000'], ['LinkedIn', 3000, 'fa-brands fa-linkedin-in', '#0A66C2'], ['TikTok', 2200, 'fa-brands fa-tiktok', '#000'], ['Pinterest', 500, 'fa-brands fa-pinterest', '#E60023'], ['YouTube', 5000, 'fa-brands fa-youtube', '#FF0000'], ['Threads', 500, 'fa-brands fa-threads', '#000'], ['Bluesky', 300, 'fa-brands fa-bluesky', '#1185FE'], ['Mastodon', 500, 'fa-brands fa-mastodon', '#6364FF']];
const s = fr ? { chars: 'Caractères', words: 'Mots', lines: 'Lignes', ph: 'Collez votre publication ici…', ok: 'OK', over: 'dépassé de', left: 'restants' } : { chars: 'Characters', words: 'Words', lines: 'Lines', ph: 'Paste your post here…', ok: 'OK', over: 'over by', left: 'left' };
---
<ToolLayout tool={tool}>
  <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1.3fr_1fr] gap-6"><div class="card p-5"><textarea id="src" rows="12" class="input" placeholder={s.ph}></textarea><div class="mt-3 flex gap-6 text-sm"><span>{s.chars}: <b id="c">0</b></span><span>{s.words}: <b id="w">0</b></span><span>{s.lines}: <b id="l">0</b></span></div></div>
    <div class="card divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800" id="limits" data-s={JSON.stringify(s)}>{limits.map(([n, max, icon, color]) => <div class="px-4 py-3 flex items-center gap-3 text-sm" data-max={max}><i class={`${icon} w-4 text-center dark:invert-0`} style={`color:${color}`}></i><span class="flex-1 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">{n}</span><span class="text-slate-400 text-xs" data-status></span><b class="w-16 text-right tabular-nums">{max}</b></div>)}</div></div>
  <script>
    const src = document.getElementById('src') as HTMLTextAreaElement; const S = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('limits')!.dataset.s!);
    const count = (s: string) => { let n = 0; for (const ch of s) n += ch.codePointAt(0)! > 0xffff ? 2 : 1; return n; };
    const render = () => { const v = src.value; const c = count(v); document.getElementById('c')!.textContent = String(c); document.getElementById('w')!.textContent = String(v.trim() ? v.trim().split(/\s+/).length : 0); document.getElementById('l')!.textContent = String(v ? v.split('\n').length : 0); document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-max]').forEach((el) => { const max = +el.dataset.max!; const st = el.querySelector('[data-status]')!; st.textContent = c > max ? `${S.over} ${c - max}` : `${max - c} ${S.left}`; st.className = `text-xs ${c > max ? 'text-rose-500 font-semibold' : 'text-slate-400'}`; }); };
    src.addEventListener('input', render); render();
  </script>
  <Fragment slot="content">{fr ? <><h2>Pourquoi les limites de caractères sur les réseaux sociaux sont-elles importantes ?</h2><p>Chaque réseau social a ses propres limites de longueur. Les dépasser peut couper votre message ou empêcher sa publication.</p><h3>Limites clés</h3><ul><li><strong>X (Twitter)</strong> : 280 caractères. Soyez concis et direct.</li><li><strong>Instagram</strong> : 2 200 caractères pour les légendes. Les hashtags comptent.</li><li><strong>LinkedIn</strong> : 3 000 caractères. Idéal pour le storytelling et le contenu long.</li><li><strong>TikTok</strong> : 2 200 caractères dans la description.</li></ul><p>Vous écrivez pour LinkedIn ? L'outil de <a href={L('/tools/mise-en-forme-texte-linkedin/')}>mise en forme de texte LinkedIn</a> ajoute gras, italique et listes. Pour mettre une seule ligne en gras, utilisez le <a href={L('/tools/generateur-texte-gras/')}>générateur de texte en gras</a>.</p></> : <><h2>Why do social media character limits matter?</h2><p>Each social media platform has its own length limits for posts. Exceeding them can cut your message off or block the post entirely.</p><h3>Key limits</h3><ul><li><strong>X (Twitter)</strong>: 280 characters. Be concise and direct.</li><li><strong>Instagram</strong>: 2,200 characters for captions. Hashtags count.</li><li><strong>LinkedIn</strong>: 3,000 characters. Ideal for storytelling and long-form content.</li><li><strong>TikTok</strong>: 2,200 characters in the description.</li></ul><p>Writing for LinkedIn? The <a href={L('/tools/linkedin-text-formatter/')}>LinkedIn text formatter</a> adds bold, italic and lists. To bold a single line on any network, use the <a href={L('/tools/bold-text-generator/')}>bold text generator</a>.</p></>}</Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
